{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he removed from there to the mountain.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he removed from that place where he had built the altar and came to Mount Moriah and built an altar a second time, to indicate that there Israel is destined to offer the burnt-offering and the peace-offerings in the Temple, and he prayed there as well to indicate (Isaiah 56) that 'My house shall be called a house of prayer for all peoples'; this is what it says: ״ויבן שם מזבח לה׳ ויקרא בשם ה׳״ — 'and he built there an altar to YHWH and called in the name of YHWH.' And what it says, ויעתק — it should have said ויעתק with a pataḥ under the tav, or ויעתק with a ṣere under the yod and the tav; but in its plain sense it means 'and he moved his tent from there to the mountain.'" "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah</b> it is possible to interpret ויעתק משם ההרה — that Abram transported, in the thoughts of his intellect, 'the mountain,' that is, the tenth sefirah called 'Mountain,' which Mount Moriah corresponds to. And this is what you find in Moses (Exodus 24): ״ויעל משה אל ההר״ — and you already know that its Targum is לטורא ('to the mountain'); and this is what it says (Exodus 19): ״ומשה עלה אל האלהים״." "<b>And behold,</b> this transport is not to separate and to cut off, heaven forbid, but to unify and to join everything as one. For he brought up to that mountain and transported it to the place of his emanation and his goings-forth, for 'his goings-forth are from of old' (מקדם), and therefore Scripture juxtaposed to it מקדם, and afterward said לבית אל — 'to Bethel' — which is Wisdom, and it is the בי״ת of בראשית, concerning which Moses praised himself (Numbers 12): ״בכל ביתי נאמן הוא״, and this is what the prophet, peace be upon him, said (Micah 4): ״לכו ונעלה אל הר ה׳ ואל בית אלהי יעקב״ — for 'the house of the God of Jacob' corresponds to 'the mountain of YHWH.' And afterward it says ״ויט אהלה״ — 'and he pitched his tent' — which is the Tent of Understanding, and therefore the word is sealed with the letter ה, which is the first ה in the Name, through which heaven and earth were created; and it is the King who built a palace by means of an architect, and the architect is the ה of בהבראם, which is the last ה in the Name. And one should contemplate the addition of the two letters ה in the word ההרה and also in the expression ויעתק, which is an expression of going forth, to allude to what I have explained; and it is further possible that ויעתק is from the expression עתיק יומין ('Ancient of Days'). And understand this." "<b>And he called in the name of YHWH.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): an expression of proclamation and publicity, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 20): ״יקרא איש חסדו״; (Psalms 116): ״ובשם ה׳ אקרא״; (Genesis 41): ״ויקראו לפניו אברך״. Its meaning is that he would publicize the divinity of the Holy One, blessed be He. And further, it may include the sense of prayer, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 30): ״אליך ה׳ אקרא ואל ה׳ אתחנן״ — for prayer pertains to mercy and supplication pertains to the attribute of justice. And so Onkelos translated: וצלי בשמא דה׳ — 'and he prayed in the name of HaShem' — and it is the great Name." "<b>And by way of the Midrash</b> it is from the expression (Psalms 104): ״המקרה במים עליותיו״ — like a man who reinforces the ceiling so that people may be secure beneath it; so Abraham would reinforce the faith in the hearts of creatures and would assure them that they would merit the life of the world to come."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :register {:flags {2 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The comment notes the unexpected vocalization of ויעתק (with a ḥataf-pataḥ under the tav in the Masoretic text) compared with the expected forms; the phonetic-grammatical descriptions are translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:14.903254111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}